content.text:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

This is a continuation of a multi-round, strict-process build of a scroll-choreographed Swedish agency landing page for "Alunix" (cell V3c), governed by CARL design-system rules, gates.md, house-physics.md, F-0xx feedback entries, and reference-lock.md's Tier-0 locked system. The conversation picked up mid-R5 (from a prior compaction) and has progressed through the end of R5 into the current round, R6.

**R6 prompt** ("Alunix r9, runda 6. Cell V3c. Fixrunda efter R5-granskningen: processakten får sin riktiga text och form."): Execute six architect-authored fix plans from `tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3c/plans/README.md § R6`, in README order: 018, 019, 020, 021, 022, 023. Key binding instructions:
- Read `plans/README.md § R6` first (plan list, order, dependencies), then every R6 plan in full (Problem/Target/Conventions/Steps/Boundaries/Verification). Grep-verify each plan's line-number anchors against the actual current code before editing; STOP and write to NOTES § R6 if code doesn't match in substance (never guess).
- Read `PROCESS-UNDERLAG.md § 3` (copy v1, verbatim) and `§ 4` (assumptions table — rows marked [A] are written per the table's stated assumption).
- Read `HELHET.md § 3` H-21 to H-35, and `reviews/r5/` (five reports) — specifically `material_fixes` and `keep` sections of each; `keep` items must never be touched.
- Load `Skill(design)` (verb build, component scope), `Skill(animate)` and `Skill(emil-design-eng)` before motion changes, `Skill(a11y-audit)` before a11y plans — all invoked by name via the Skill tool, named in transcript.
- Execute plans in README order, running each plan's own Verification before opening the next; report outcome in transcript AND in NOTES § R6 as exactly one of `verified` / `best-effort` (naming what remains) / `reverted` (naming why) — never `verified` on feel alone.
- Surgical `Edit` calls only, never `Write` of the whole file, never shell-writes against UI files. Engine (`scroll/*.js`) and `sites/*` never touched. Never touch anything in the five reports' `keep` lists: `--sc-ps` contract (staircase 0), `will-change` only via class, sticky as the sole height mechanism, `pathLength="1"` with `*1px`, the `@property` registrations, iframe `inert`+`pointer-events:none`, `<ol>` with text in DOM regardless of opacity.
- Copy v1 written verbatim from the underlag § 3 (step titles, paragraphs, marginal rows, principles, ledger rows), marked `<!-- copy v1, copy-gate i R7 -->`. Locked copy (15 strings — actually 18 individual strings per prior rounds' count) never touched. Zero em-dashes. No numbers beyond the drawing's own measurements and the locked prices. The `7 rem` measurement corrected per plan 020 (the line should show what the callout claims).
- After the LAST plan, run the full mechanical grind in-session: (1) `motion_probe.py --cpu 4` on both `section.hero:--sc-ps,.plate-card:transform` and `#process:--sc-ps,#p-outline:stroke-dashoffset,#p-opening:stroke-dashoffset`, both `--wheel 100:60` and `--wheel 20:120`, and also `--cpu 1`; report control-vs-page side by side; bar: staircase 0, p95≤20ms, 0 frames>33ms, `--sc-ps` max_step≤3%; if frame-time still fails, report numbers BEFORE and AFTER the perf plans (018), not just after. (2) `scroll_verify.py` at 1440×900 and 390×844, output to `shots/r6`; check H-16/H-17/H-18. (3) `perf_probe.py --cpu 4` at 1440 and 390: `long-task-under-scroll` 0, CLS≤0.05, page's own weight. (4) `preflight_taste.py`, `detect.mjs --json`, `contrast_over_media.py --url` (frame captions, paper under the ark, card back), `a11y_scan.py`, `tab_walk.py`, `reflow.py`, PLUS explicitly at 900×600, 1024×640, 1180×740, 1280×800, 1366×640 (ark clipping/folding). (5) Grep: `prefers-reduced-motion` 0, U+2013/U+2014 0 in visible text, no new inline-hex. (6) Screenshots: `?preview=process-01…07` at 1440 and 390, twelve-frame sequence through the act at 1440 and 390, heron at `--flip` 0/0.25/0.5/0.75/1, whole page in slices at 1440 and 390, fold at 320/375/414/768/1024/1280 — all into `shots/r6/`, each read as pixels with `läst: <fil>` in NOTES, F-007 graded frame-by-frame against each plan's target table. (7) The PageDown walk from a11y fix 3: all seven steps must render; report the outcome.
- Invariants: F-011 (motion always plays, no `prefers-reduced-motion`), F-014 (everything that moves reads `--sc-ps`), gates 47/79/75/88, `PRODUCT.md § absences`, `@property` for every `--p-*`, one height mechanism, no third iframe, no generation. Full output required; if forced to pause, end with `[PAUSED — plan X]` as the last line.
- Delivery: `index.html`, `shots/r6/`, `NOTES.md § R6` (one row per plan with verdict, the grind with control/page numbers, the F-007 table, the PageDown outcome, locked copy 15/15, deviations with reasons), `BRIEF.md § decision ledger` (rows the plans specify). Final message's last line: `R6 klar` or `[PAUSED — plan X]`.

A system-level directive ("CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY...") then interrupted the session mid-Plan-023-verification, demanding this summary with no further tool calls — this is the reason Plans 023's final confirmation, and the entire post-plans grind/NOTES/BRIEF work, has not yet been completed.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - CSS scroll-choreography engine "scrollcraft" (vendored, never edited): publishes raw `--sc-p` per `[data-sc-act]` element; the co-located separate shim `sc-smooth.js` publishes a lerped, registered (`@property`, `inherits:true`) `--sc-ps` that all bespoke motion must read (F-014).
   - `data-sc-act="flow"` acts (as opposed to `pin`): `#process` and `#principer` are both `flow` acts now, no longer using the engine's own pin mechanism for height (that's page-authored CSS instead, per plan 019's formbeslut).
   - New in R6: a **step-relative progress variable system** (`--k1..--k7`), each `clamp(0,calc((var(--sc-ps,0)-var(--sN))/(var(--eN)-var(--sN))),1)`, declared as ordinary (unregistered, thus `inherits:true`) custom properties on `#process`, replacing R5's direct-`--sc-ps`-window system. Per-bana windows are now `[a,b]` FRACTIONS of their own step's 0-1 `--kN` range, not absolute `--sc-ps` fractions.
   - **Anchored scroll windows**: instead of a fixed table of `--sc-ps` fractions per step (R5's design), R6's plan 019 computes each step's window (`--s1..--e7`) ONCE at runtime from the ACTUAL rendered position of each `<li>` in the document flow (`measureAct`), via `process.style.setProperty('--sN', ...)` — CSS carries only a no-JS fallback.
   - **Cumulative, one-way `data-on` group toggling**: `<g data-step="0N">` SVG groups get `display:none` until `--sc-ps` (via `processPs()`, a cheap JS approximation) crosses that step's own `s` threshold, then stay visible for the rest of the forward scroll (and hide again if scrolled back above threshold) — implements "earlier marks stay drawn as you scroll forward" plus bidirectional erase, while keeping un-reached banor out of the style tree (perf finding 3).
   - **Paint-order vs. logical-step-order tension**: SVG paints in document order; `g[data-step="05"]` (the Calyx image) had to be placed FIRST in the DOM (before 01-04/07) so the image paints under `#p-opening`'s contour, breaking the assumption that `sheetGroups` array-indexing matches step order — required a step-number-KEYED lookup in JS instead of positional indexing (a deliberate, documented deviation from the plan's literal code snippet).
   - CSS Grid `grid-template-columns: minmax(300px,384px) minmax(0,880px)` for the new two-column `.process-grid` (steps left, sticky ark right) — discovered to genuinely under-render the second column (825.6px, not 880px) at the canonical 1440px viewport once `padding-inline:var(--rail-x)` and `column-gap` are subtracted, causing "true measurement" claims (7rem, 96px) to read short by the same ~6.2% scale factor; pure-ratio claims (16:9) remain exact.
   - CSS `position:sticky` used TWICE now with different roles: `.process-stick` (desktop, sticky beside flowing text) and, under `@media(max-width:1279px)`, repositioned via `order:-1` to sit ABOVE the text, `top:0`.
   - `color-mix(in srgb, ...)` for the numerals' fill tone-byte (accent → `--hair-ink` over step 6's `--k6`), and for an opacity dip (`1 - 0.3*var(--k5)`) during Calyx's reveal — both multiplicative with the existing fade-in `--p-t`, not replacing it.
   - `stroke-dashoffset` + `pathLength="1"` + explicit `*1px` unit dash-draw technique (K3-derived), with a "snap opacity" (`clamp(0,calc(var(--p-l)*9999),1)`) to hide SVG markers that render on path vertices regardless of `stroke-dashoffset` progress (an R5 finding, re-applied to the new `#p-glyph` path).
   - `content-visibility:hidden` (toggled via a persistent, never-`unobserve`d IntersectionObserver at `rootMargin:'40% 0px'`) to sleep off-screen iframe wrappers without touching `transform`/`opacity` (preserving the "never transform/tint a shown frame" PRODUCT.md rule) — plan 018's core mechanism, replacing R4/R5's one-shot-mount-then-detach observer.
   - `inert` + focus-parking pattern for the card-flip's currently-hidden face: `setFace()` now checks `hiding.contains(document.activeElement)` and calls `heroPlate.focus({preventScroll:true})` BEFORE setting `inert`, to prevent Chromium's focus-reset-to-`body` behavior when an ancestor becomes inert.
   - `.sr-only` visually-hidden-but-AT-accessible pattern (standard clip-rect technique) used to expose the card-back's four locked strings to screen readers even while the visual face is `inert` (Chromium hides `inert` subtrees from AT entirely, so a live sibling copy is needed).
   - `previewFace` authoritative-override pattern: lets `?preview=` modes win over the scroll-driven `setFace(ps>=0.44)` call inside `readState`, fixing a bug where scrolling to top after a preview-forced state would silently re-hide the previewed face.
   - Algebraic verification of scroll-target formulas: derived (and fixed) the mobile preview-scroll formula by solving `measureAct`'s own `e = (yc + 0.5*(vh+sheetH))/life` for `scrollY`, proving the correct offset needs `+sheetH/2` not `-sheetH/2`.
   - `sc-smooth.js`'s lerp settling time: confirmed that after a single large `window.scrollTo()` jump, the smoothed `--sc-ps` needs ~1000ms (not 200ms) to fully converge to the raw target — relevant to any short-wait verification script.
   - Empirical re-derivation of the `--scrub` window (plan 023) via Playwright bisection search when the plan's own cited numbers proved to deviate from measured reality by far more than the plan's own stated 0.05 tolerance (0.62/0.95 assumed vs. 0.364/0.679 measured).
   - `motion_probe.py`'s known tool limitations (both pre-documented in the round's own README "Grindar och verktyg" section, confirmed by me not to require fixing this round): (a) `atan2(b,a)` decoding falls back to reading translation for a pure `scale()` transform, reporting DEAD on `.giant`/`#threadFill`; (b) `clip-path` can't be parsed as a numeric track at all ("för få mätpunkter"). `scroll_verify.py`'s 64×36 downsample under-detects sparse hairline/text content, producing false-positive low-diff readings — documented pattern, reconfirmed in R6.
   - WCAG 2.2 AA criteria: 1.4.3/1.4.11 (contrast, text and non-text), 2.4.3 (focus order), 2.5.8 (target size), 1.3.1 (info/relationships — sr-only card-back copy).

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`tests/alunix-r8/runs/V3c/index.html`** — the single build artifact, the only file edited this round (plus, cumulatively from earlier rounds, four shared tool scripts, unchanged in R6 itself). Extensive rewrites across R6:
     - **Plan 018** (`.frame-wrap`/`.calyx-wrap`/`.horai-wrap`/observer/reveal-attribute lines): added `.frame-wrap.is-asleep{content-visibility:hidden;}` and `will-change:auto` on `.frame-wrap`; rewrote the IntersectionObserver:
       ```js
       var io = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries){
         for (var i = 0; i < entries.length; i++){
           var f = entries[i].target, wrap = f.parentNode;
           if (entries[i].isIntersecting){
             wrap.classList.remove('is-asleep');
             if (f.hasAttribute('data-src')) defer(mountFrame.bind(null, f));
           } else if (!f.hasAttribute('data-src')){
             wrap.classList.add('is-asleep');
           }
         }
       }, { rootMargin: '40% 0px' });
       ```
